<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Duchy of Saxe-Coburg</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1572">1572</a>–<a href="/years/1633">1633</a>; <a href="/years/1680">1680</a>–<a href="/years/1699">1699</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Duchy of Saxe-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coburg">Coburg</a> was an Ernestine <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxons">Saxon</a> duchy centred on Coburg in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/franconia">Franconia</a>. It first existed under Duke John Casimir until 1633, and was revived in 1680 when the lands of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ernest-i-duke-of-saxe-gotha">Ernest the Pious</a> were divided among his sons. When its duke Albert died without heirs in 1699, a long dispute followed, and most of Coburg passed to Saxe-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saalfeld">Saalfeld</a>, forming Saxe-Coburg-Saalfeld.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/duchy-of-saxe-coburg.jpg" alt="Duchy of Saxe-Coburg" width="320" height="280" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sir Iain · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Locator_Duchy_of_Saxe-Coburg_(1680).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
